What it does
•	Registration: a user signs up with email and password, gets a 6-digit code by email (valid 10 minutes, stored hashed), and the account activates once the code is entered. Passwords are hashed with bcrypt, and login uses a JWT.
•	Payment: the user picks eDahab or ZAAD and enters a phone number, and the server creates the payment through Sifalopay. A purchase is granted only when Sifalopay confirms it as paid, and you configure the webhook URL on their side.
•	Reading only: when you upload a PDF, the server converts each page to an image and keeps the original PDF private. Pages load only for users who bought the book (or admins), and the reader shows them as a page-turning flipbook. There is no download link to the PDF, and right-click and save shortcuts are blocked in the reader.
•	Admin dashboard: the admin can upload a PDF with title, author, description and price, delete books, and see user count, paid orders, revenue and sales per book.
•	Free preview: page 1 of every book is public and used as the cover.
To run it
1.	Install Node 18+ and poppler-utils (it provides the pdftoppm converter).
2.	Copy .env.example to .env and fill it in (SMTP, Sifalopay key, admin login, JWT secret).
3.	Run npm install, then npm start.
4.	Open http://localhost:3000.
For the webhook to work, the server must be reachable over HTTPS at PUBLIC_URL.
